# Cisco One Experience Lab — local memory

dCloud **PseudoCo / Cisco One** lab. Client VPN must be up before SSH or playbooks. Topology and access lookup live in `Lab Topology/`. Do not put passwords in playbooks or unencrypted inventory.

## Workflow

- Author playbooks on the Mac in this repo. Do not write new playbooks on Kali.
- Commit/push only when the user asks. Remote: `https://github.com/imanassypov/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation` (`main`, public).
- Test on the Kali script server after it has `main` at `~/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation`.
- Mac refresh (VPN up): `ansible-automation/00_scriptserver_bootstrap` venv, then `playbooks/01_bootstrap_script_server.yml` (also git-pulls) or `playbooks/02_sync_from_git.yml` (git only).
- On Kali, Ansible is on PATH from `~/venv`. Recreate `.vault` there if a collection needs Vault (gitignored).

## Script server

- Kali Linux at `198.18.134.12`. SSH user and passwords come from Vault (`inventory/group_vars/script_servers/vault.yml`), unlocked by gitignored `.vault`.
- Mac controller: project `.venv` via `setup-local-venv.sh`; `ansible_connection: paramiko`.
- Only project tree on Kali: `~/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation`. Never create `~/cisco-one-automation`.

## Collections

- Playbooks live under `ansible-automation/`, numbered by lab-build order: `00_scriptserver_bootstrap`, `01_campus`, `02_data_center`, `03_dmz`, `04_remote_dc`, `05_sdwan`, `06_secure_access`.
- Inside each collection, playbooks are `00_`, `01_`, … in apply order.
- `00_` is implemented. `01_`–`06_` are stubs until built.
